From: Yoonji Park <koreapyj@dcmys.kr>
Subject: [PATCH] uqmid: ModemManager style modem management over ubus

Turn uqmid into a daemon which owns the QMI control device and exposes
the modem over ubus, with objects, states and behaviour following
ModemManager:

- build fixes and fixes for the existing state machines, request
  timeouts, per client indication dispatch and client id handling
- wwan subsystem control devices next to USB cdc-wdm devices
- modem object: states, enable/disable, power state, reset, own
  numbers, extended signal information, cell info, modes and bands,
  capabilities and the profile manager
- SIM objects, SIM hot swap and carrier configuration (PDC)
- 3GPP registration, bearers (including P-CSCF addresses and IMS
  profile flags) and the Simple interface
- voice calls with call end reasons, and SMS messaging
- extension methods for QMI features without a ModemManager equivalent

See uqmid/README.md for the ubus API.
