+/*
+ * uqmid -- allowed/preferred modes and bands
+ *
+ * ModemManager 1.24.2: Modem.SupportedModes, CurrentModes, SupportedBands, CurrentBands and the methods
+ * SetCurrentModes, SetCurrentBands. Sources: mm-iface-modem.c (interface_initialization_step(),
+ * mm_iface_modem_set_current_modes(), mm_iface_modem_set_current_bands(), handle_set_current_modes(),
+ * handle_set_current_bands()), mm-shared-qmi.c (load_current_capabilities, load_supported_modes,
+ * load_current_modes, set_current_modes, load_supported_bands, load_current_bands, set_current_bands) and
+ * mm-modem-helpers-qmi.c (the translations between QMI and the MM mode and band values).
+ *
+ * Properties of the modem object (the MM values are bit masks and numbers, here they are the nicks of the MM
+ * enums):
+ *  - supported_modes: [{allowed: [...], preferred: "..."}], current_modes: {allowed: [...], preferred: "..."}.
+ *    Mode nicks: "cs", "2g", "3g", "4g", "5g", "any"; preferred is one nick or "none".
+ *  - supported_bands / current_bands: ["egsm", "utran-1", "eutran-3", "ngran-78", ...] (the nicks of MMModemBand),
+ *    "unknown" while the bands are not known.
+ *
+ * Methods (state changing: through the serialized operations, MM: mm_base_modem_authorize_and_operation_lock()):
+ *  - set_current_modes {allowed: [...], preferred: "..."}
+ *  - set_current_bands {bands: [...]}
+ *
+ * Initialization (MM: interface_initialization_step(), steps CURRENT_CAPABILITIES (the features and the radio
+ * interfaces, load_current_capabilities of mm-shared-qmi.c), SUPPORTED_CAPABILITIES, SUPPORTED_MODES,
+ * SUPPORTED_BANDS, CURRENT_MODES, CURRENT_BANDS). They are steps of the initialization of the modem (modem_fsm.c)
+ * in the order of MM: the capabilities right after the version info (before the identity of the modem), the supported
+ * modes and bands after it, the current modes and bands after the power state and before the SIM steps. Like in MM:
+ *  - a failure of the capabilities (DMS Get Capabilities fails, the modem has no current capabilities, no NAS or DMS
+ *    client) fails the initialization: "Failed to load current capabilities: ..." is MM_CORE_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED, which
+ *    mm-broadband-modem.c iface_modem_initialize_ready() turns into the state "failed" with the failed reason
+ *    "unknown-capabilities"; the later steps are not run;
+ *  - NAS SSP and NAS TP both failing is not an error: both features stay unsupported (and are not asked again);
+ *  - the failures of the other steps are not critical (only logged, the properties keep their defaults: supported modes
+ *    "any", current modes "any", bands "unknown") and what is loaded is not loaded again; the initialization steps run
+ *    again after an unlock (mm-iface-modem.c), here uqmid_modes_bands_load() does it for the supported and current
+ *    modes and bands.
+ *
+ * Deviations from MM:
+ *  - A set request which gets its turn while the steps run again after an unlock waits for them.
+ *  - A MM band without a nick in the MM enum (e.g. EUTRAN 15) is not listed in the properties (MM prints the
+ *    number); it is still used internally.
+ *  - "an extended LTE/NR5G band list is reported" is "the list is not empty" (the QMI parser does not tell an
+ *    empty TLV from a missing one).
+ *
+ * Capabilities: current_capabilities ([nicks of MMModemCapability]) and supported_capabilities ([[nicks], ...], the
+ * combinations of mm_supported_capabilities_from_qmi_supported_capabilities_context()) and the method
+ * set_current_capabilities {capabilities: [nicks]} (mm_iface_modem.c handle_set_current_capabilities_auth_ready(),
+ * mm_shared_qmi_set_current_capabilities()).
+ */
