+/*
+ * uqmid -- extended signal information (ModemManager: Modem.Signal, mm_iface_modem_signal_* in
+ * mm-iface-modem-signal.c and the "Load extended signal information", "Setup threshold values" and
+ * nas_signal_info_indication_cb() parts of mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c)
+ *
+ * Methods of the modem object:
+ *  - signal_setup {rate}: MM Setup(). Refresh rate in seconds, 0 disables the periodic refresh.
+ *  - signal_setup_thresholds {rssi_threshold, error_rate_threshold}: MM SetupThresholds().
+ *  - signal_get: the properties of the MM interface (Rate, Threshold, ErrorRateThreshold, Cdma, Evdo, Gsm, Umts,
+ *    Lte, Nr5g).
+ * Notification of the modem object: signal.updated (same content as signal_get), sent when a property changed.
+ *
+ * Values (mm_signal_get_dictionary()): a technology which has no values is not in the reply (MM: empty
+ * dictionary), and a value which is not known (MM_SIGNAL_UNKNOWN) is left out of its table. All values are doubles
+ * in dBm / dB. The keys are rssi, rscp, ecio, sinr, io, rsrp, rsrq, snr and error_rate.
+ *
+ * Like in MM the interface is only active while the modem is enabled (common_enable_disable(): it is enabled after
+ * messaging and before voice, disabled after voice). The rate and the thresholds survive a disable, the values are
+ * reset (check_interface_reset()). Values are published (and the polling runs) only while the interface is enabled
+ * and a rate or a threshold is set (mm_iface_modem_signal_update()).
+ *
+ * Deviations from MM:
+ *  - the RSSI of the Get Signal Strength RSSI list is an unsigned magnitude in QMI (-dBm): it is negated here, MM
+ *    reports the unsigned value as it is;
+ *  - 5G values of -32768 (QMI: not connected) are not reported (MM reports them);
+ *  - the query which MM runs after the thresholds were configured is skipped while the interface is disabled (its
+ *    result would be dropped).
+ */
