+/*
+ * uqmid -- voice calls (ModemManager: Modem.Voice + Call, mm-iface-modem-voice.c, mm-base-call.c,
+ * mm-call-qmi.c, mm-call-list.c and the Voice parts of mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c)
+ *
+ * The modem object has the voice_* methods (ListCalls, CreateCall, DeleteCall, HangupAll, HoldAndAccept,
+ * HangupAndAccept, Transfer, CallWaitingSetup, CallWaitingQuery). Every call is an ubus object of its own
+ * (uqmid.modem.<N>.call.<M>) with the methods start, accept, deflect, hangup, send_dtmf and get.
+ *
+ * QMI: one VOICE client is allocated when the modem is initialized and kept for the life time of the modem (MM:
+ * qmi_services[] in mm-broadband-modem-qmi.c, mm_shared_qmi_ensure_client()): a call ends when the client which
+ * dialed it is released (see docs/voice-call-audio.md of the device). Enabling registers the call and the
+ * supplementary service notification events (common_voice_enable_disable_unsolicited_events()); disabling only
+ * unregisters the indications, matching mm_iface_modem_voice_disable().
+ * The call list is driven by the All Call Status indication (all_call_status_indication_cb()
+ * -> mm_iface_modem_voice_report_all_calls()), no polling (MM_IFACE_MODEM_VOICE_PERIODIC_CALL_LIST_CHECK_DISABLED).
+ *
+ * Deviations from MM:
+ *  - voice_create_call needs an enabled modem (the indications are only registered then);
+ *  - DeleteCall hangs up a call which is not terminated yet (best effort), MM just drops the object;
+ *  - a call in the All Call Status indication without a Remote Party Number entry is reported without number
+ *    (MM would drop it from the report, which terminates the known call);
+ *  - the EF_ECC numbers of the SIM are not read: with a SIM only 112 and 911 are emergency numbers;
+ *  - multiparty (join/leave) and deflecting are not supported (MM: join/leave use Manage Calls, deflect is AT
+ *    only), the "multiparty" property is always false;
+ *  - audio_port and audio_format are empty: the audio of a call is a separate ALSA card (out of scope).
+ *
+ * uqmid extensions (MM has none of them: all_call_status_indication_cb() ignores the call end reason of the
+ * QMI indication and always reports MM_CALL_STATE_REASON_UNKNOWN for a terminated call, so state_reason is
+ * kept as MM has it):
+ *  - end_reason {value, name}: the QMI VOICE call end reason (QmiVoiceCallEndReason, nick names of libqmi) of a
+ *    call, from the Call End Reason TLV of the All Call Status indication; for a call hung up by a request of
+ *    the user (hangup, voice_hangup_all, ...) it is client-end, until the indication tells otherwise. Shown by
+ *    `get` once known and in the notifications of the transition to terminated.
+ *  - cc_cause: the TS 24.008 Annex H cause value of the call, from the Raw Call End Cause Code TLV (0x35) of the
+ *    All Call Status indication; only present when the modem sent it for the call.
+ */
